From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arsslen Idadi <arsslens021@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 08:20:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] pam: Start Amethystora's duress action on the duress
 finger

With duress=allow or duress=deny, read the account's duress finger from
its line in /etc/amethystora/duress.d/fingers, and when a reader that
identified reports that finger as the match, call Run on the
org.amethystora.Duress service of the system bus, without waiting for
an answer and without starting the service. With allow the finger then
logs in like any other; with deny it is refused exactly as a finger
that did not match, and the module asks again.

The file is ignored unless it and its folder are root's and nobody else
may read them. A reader that verified a single finger it chose itself
never counts, nor does a daemon that does not name the matched finger.
Nothing about the duress finger is logged, with debug or without.

duress-dir= points the module at another folder, for the tests, which
run as root only: as anyone else the file is never trusted.
